These apply-patch scenarios are ported from OpenAI Codex
(https://github.com/openai/codex, codex-rs/apply-patch/tests/fixtures/scenarios,
commit 4d3ed3f3b47d39f8fe0b60df74a20f528b6fc618), licensed under the Apache License 2.0.

Layout per scenario: input/ (initial files), patch.txt, expected/ (exact final state).

Deliberate difference: Tugline applies a patch all-or-nothing, so scenario 015
was renamed from 015_failure_after_partial_success_leaves_changes to
015_failure_after_partial_success_leaves_no_changes and its expected/ state is empty
(Codex leaves created.txt behind when a later hunk fails).

Ambiguity: Codex applies a hunk at the FIRST matching location. Tugline refuses a
hunk whose lines match more than one place in its search region (after the previous
hunk and the optional @@ anchor) and lists the candidate line numbers. None of the
scenarios here relies on first-match (all of them have a unique hunk location), so no
scenario needed changing for this; the refusal is covered by test/edit-patch.test.ts
("A7/A1: an ambiguous hunk is refused …").
